    "originalText": "1.6 Discoverability\nThe video library design features a predictable structure by providing clear, easy-to-use navigation and filtering tools that help users quickly narrow down available content. Filters are visible and intuitive, allowing users to browse the library based on relevant criteria without having to search through large amounts of content manually. The consistent layout and predictable filtering patterns make it easy to refine results, adjust selections, and explore different content, creating an efficient and user-friendly browsing experience.\nEducators can quickly narrow search results using easy-to-use filters for grade level, subject, topic, standards, and video length. This makes it simple to find relevant content that aligns with specific classroom needs and professional learning goals.",
    "revisedText": "1.6 Discoverability\n\nThe library provides search and visible filters to help educators find relevant classroom examples. Users can explore content by grade, subject, topic, or duration and review the resulting video cards before choosing a resource.\nStandards filtering is available with the appropriate license. Use the standards selector to explore aligned content; do not assume it combines with every other filter.",
