    "revisedNotes": "5.1 Assessment Alignment\n\nScope: Teaching Channel Video Platform. Evidence review dated September 22, 2026.\n\nReviewer walkthrough\nPair an instructional goal with a populated feedback example. The supplied general-feedback screenshot has empty fields. Acknowledgement completion was not tested.\n\nEvidence basis\nEducator feedback thread; rendered slide 38; Views/ActivityCenter/_GeneralFeedbackPanel.cshtml:12; _AcknowledgeFeedbackPanel.cshtml:8\n\nBefore submission\nShow a populated goal-to-feedback example; the current form screenshot is empty.\n\nThese notes describe evidence and verification limits; they are not an ISTE approval or a substitute for the official indicator requirements.",
    "originalText": "5.1 Assessment Alignment\nTeaching Channel’s video coaching tools provide an ongoing, formative approach to assessing instructional practice. Educators set an instructional goal, upload a video of their teaching, and submit it for evaluation and feedback aligned to that goal or instructional framework. Educators can then reflect on the feedback, apply it in their practice, and submit future videos to demonstrate progress, creating a continuous cycle of assessment, feedback, and growth.\nIn this example, educators submit a video of their instruction to receive targeted feedback aligned with their professional goals.\nThis section allows coaches to provide overall feedback, identify next steps, and recommend relevant resources. Educators acknowledge the feedback, making it easy to track progress and apply recommendations to future lessons.",
    "revisedText": "5.1 Assessment Alignment\n\nVideo coaching supports formative review of instructional practice. An educator documents a goal and shares a relevant artifact; an eligible coach can connect observations and feedback to that goal or an available framework.\nA later artifact and reflection can support a follow-up discussion about changes in practice.\nIn this example, educators submit a video of their instruction to receive targeted feedback aligned with their professional goals.\nThe general-feedback form includes strengths, areas for growth, and next steps. A completed example is needed to demonstrate how feedback connects to the educator’s goal.",
